## Troubleshooting

### Fit Issues
- **Too Tight**: Reduce diameter by 0.1–0.2mm and regenerate
- **Too Loose**: Increase diameter by 0.1–0.2mm and regenerate
- **Unstable**: Check grid mounting points for debris; clean and retry

### Print Quality
- **Layer Adhesion Failure**: Increase bed temperature +5°C; reduce first layer speed to 15 mm/s
- **Warping**: Increase bed temperature +5°C; ensure heated bed is level
- **Under-Extrusion**: Check nozzle is not clogged; verify filament path is smooth

### Material-Specific
- **PLA**: Brittle if printed cold; ensure nozzle ≥200°C
- **PETG**: Prone to stringing; increase retraction distance by 1–2mm
- **TPU**: Extrude slowly; reduce speed to 25 mm/s; use flexible nozzle (PTFE-free ideally)

## Maintenance

- **Cleaning**: Wipe with damp cloth (avoid soaking)
- **Storage**: Keep away from heat (PLA deforms >60°C)
- **Replacement**: Regenerate and reprint if worn or damaged

